{
  "Article, a longer write-up with numbered sections": {
    "prefix": "template-article",
    "description": "manuscript article template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: article.with(",
      "  title: [${1:The Title}],",
      "  course: \"${2:CS 173}\",",
      "  date: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "",
      "= ${3:Introduction}",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "Book, a whole course's notes with cover and contents": {
    "prefix": "template-book",
    "description": "manuscript book template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: book.with(",
      "  title: [${1:The Title}],",
      "  code: \"${2:CS 173}\",",
      "  university: \"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\",",
      "  date: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "",
      "= ${3:First Chapter}",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "One-page exam cheat sheet, three columns": {
    "prefix": "template-cheatsheet",
    "description": "manuscript cheatsheet template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: cheatsheet.with(course: \"${1:CS 173}\", title: \"${2:Exam 1}\")",
      "",
      "= ${3:Topic}",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "Essay in the house style (main.typ that includes body.typ)": {
    "prefix": "template-essay",
    "description": "manuscript essay template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: essay.with(",
      "  title: \"${1:The Title}\",",
      "  course: \"${2:RHET 105}\",",
      "  date: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "#include \"${3:body.typ}\"",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "Homework or problem set to hand in": {
    "prefix": "template-homework",
    "description": "manuscript homework template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: homework.with(",
      "  course: \"${1:CS 173}\",",
      "  title: \"${2:Problem Set}\",",
      "  number: ${3:1},",
      "  netid: \"ae42\",",
      "  due: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "",
      "= Question 1",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "Lab report (from the vault's _Templates/lab-report.typ)": {
    "prefix": "template-lab",
    "description": "manuscript lab template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: lab.with(",
      "  course: \"${1:PHYS 211}\",",
      "  number: ${2:1},",
      "  title: \"${3:The Title of the Lab}\",",
      "  authors: (\"Alejandro Escamilla\", \"Partner One\", \"Partner Two\"),",
      "  data: \"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/...\",  // link to the shared data sheet",
      "  date: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "",
      "= Introduction",
      "",
      "The purpose of this experiment is to #todo[state the goal].",
      "",
      "= Methods",
      "",
      "Procedure:",
      "+ #todo[First step]",
      "+ #todo[Second step]",
      "",
      "#figure(",
      "  rect(width: 60%, height: 2in)[#todo[photo of the setup or FBD: image(\"setup.png\", width: 60%)]],",
      "  caption: [The experimental setup.],",
      ") <fig:setup>",
      "",
      "= Results",
      "",
      "#todo[IOLab graphs and the spreadsheet graph. Annotate at least one IOLab graph.]",
      "",
      "// An IOLab or spreadsheet export, read from a CSV next to this file:",
      "// #data-table(csv(\"run1.csv\"), caption: [Run 1], limit: 20)",
      "",
      "= Analysis",
      "",
      "Formulas used:",
      "\\$ F_\"net\" = sum F = m a \\$ <eq:newton>",
      "",
      "#todo[Interpret the curves, citing @eq:newton and @fig:setup.]",
      "",
      "= Discussion",
      "",
      "Theoretical model (predictions): #todo[what the theory predicts, as equations]",
      "",
      "Compare the results to the model, explain discrepancies, and justify decisions.",
      "// e.g. a measured #qty(\"9.70\", \\$m\\\\/s^2\\$, err: \"0.05\") is #percent-error(9.70, 9.81) off from #qty(\"9.81\", \\$m\\\\/s^2\\$).",
      "",
      "= Conclusion",
      "",
      "#todo[Summarize findings.]",
      "",
      "#contributions((",
      "  \"Alejandro Escamilla\": todo[what they did],",
      "  \"Partner One\": todo[what they did],",
      "  \"Partner Two\": todo[what they did],",
      "))"
    ]
  },
  "MLA-format essay (main.typ that includes body.typ)": {
    "prefix": "template-mla",
    "description": "manuscript mla template",
    "isFileTemplate": true,
    "body": [
      "#import \"@local/manuscript:0.20.0\" as manuscript: *",
      "",
      "#show: mla.with(",
      "  title: \"${1:The Title}\",",
      "  instructor: \"${2:Professor Doe}\",",
      "  course: \"${3:ENG 101}\",",
      "  date: datetime(year: $CURRENT_YEAR, month: $CURRENT_MONTH, day: $CURRENT_DATE),",
      ")",
      "#include \"${4:body.typ}\"",
      "$0"
    ]
  },
  "Lecture notes, one lecture per file": {
